h1 Draw a Play
p.lead Lay players and officials out on a field, draw their movement, and share the result as a link.

.draw-toolbar
  //- Populated client-side by app.js: the Select/Arrow tool toggle, the
  //- preset groups (Formations, Situations), the marker palette, and Undo.
  //- The share button (Task 7) still lands here later; left empty in markup
  //- either way, since none of this can be rendered server-side (see the
  //- noscript note below).

.draw-board-wrap
  svg#board.draw-board

//- The board is built entirely client-side from lib/field/ and lib/draw/, so
//- with no JavaScript this page is a blank white box. A default board isn't
//- rendered server-side instead, because a shared link's state lives in the
//- URL fragment (Task 7), which never reaches the server — a no-JS rendering
//- would silently show the wrong play rather than none at all.
noscript
  p This page draws in your browser and needs JavaScript. For the same diagrams as static images, see #[a(href='/information/') Information].

script(type='module' src='/js/draw/app.js')
